# msgspec HTTP Boundary (ADR-026 / F11)

Traces to `[Corpus: adr]` ADR-026, `[Corpus: api]` serialization table, E10-28.

## High-churn routes

High-churn **msgspec response** routes:

- `POST /api/v1/convert`, `/convert-zip`, `/convert-bulletin`, `/validate`, `/lint-tac`,
  `/decode-tac` (multipart Form/File intake unchanged)
- `GET /api/v1/lint-issue-catalog` (JSON GET; msgspec response encode — E11-31)
- `POST /api/v1/dissemination/preflight`, `/dissemination/send` (JSON body; msgspec —
  E14-07=A / ADR-030)

| Layer | Technology |
|-------|------------|
| Request intake | FastAPI **`Form` / `File`** multipart — **unchanged** |
| After assemble | Optional **msgspec Struct** validation of assembled fields |
| Response encode | **msgspec** |
| OpenAPI | Thin **pydantic** aliases / JSON Schema export only — **no** dual runtime validation |

## Do not

- Claim msgspec JSON-decodes the multipart body (`msgspec.json.decode` on raw form bytes).
- Put msgspec on auth / admin / work-sessions routes — those stay **pydantic**.
- Dual-run pydantic + msgspec response validation on the same path.

## Do

- Keep packages (`tac2iwxxm`, `tac-validate`, `iwxxm-validate`) on msgspec IR/reports (ADR-016).
- Update FE OpenAPI/client types in the **same cycle** when response shapes break.
- Re-run H4–H5 after Render redeploy when F11 HTTP contract changes
  ([connectivity-gates.md](../../skills/connectivity-gates.md)).

Raise `[Contradiction]` if code or docs say msgspec validates multipart request bodies directly.
